======================================================================================
INTERPRETATION
======================================================================================
• Rows with the same color everywhere → effect is uniform across
  basins for that residue.
• Columns with the same color everywhere → effect is uniform across
  residues for that basin (the universality test).
• If β-branched residues (red labels) stand out from the rest,
  the rotamer effect is branching-driven, not universal.
• If the patterns are identical across all residues, the lever
  story is a clean universal mechanical coupling.
